```
#include <cmath>

double voltage(V), current(A);
double power, resistance;

power = voltage * current;
resistance = power / current;

cout << "Power: " << power << endl;
cout << "Resistance: " << resistance << endl;
```
Note that this function assumes that the power is calculated using the formula `power = voltage * current`. The resistance is calculated using the formula `resistance = power / current`.

